WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.550
With DreamWorks' Trolls movie out on Blu-ray
and DVD now, it's time to take a look at some

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.250
intriguing deleted scenes that were cut from
the final version of the movie.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.490
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video I'm going to review and

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.430
explain the scenes from Trolls that we didn't
see in the movie.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:19.611
Quick warning: there are spoilers here if
you haven't seen the film already, so if you

00:00:19.611 --> 00:00:24.340
want to avoid those, tap or click here to
watch my spoiler-free review of the movie.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.600
King Peppy was initially going to hand over
his crown to Princess Poppy much earlier in

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.660
the movie and we get an indication of this
in a deleted scene from the beginning of the

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.460
film which takes place after the Trolls have
escaped from Bergen Town and Poppy is grown

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.840
up.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.839
King Peppy is listening to Poppy tell the
young trolls the story of the trolls and the

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:46.120
Bergens and when she finishes, he asks her
'what happened to the brave King Peppy?'

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.280
In this scene we see that Peppy has become
rather absent-minded and confused as he's

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.769
grown older; in the final movie they dialled
back that aspect of the character.

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:59.909
And because his memory isn't so good in this
deleted version, he plans to pass on his crown

00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:03.370
to Princess Poppy so she can become the new
leader of the trolls.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:07.460
Also as Poppy's coronation was originally
going to be a much bigger event in the movie,

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.320
she was going to need a special coronation
dress.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.070
In fact, the dress was the focus of a cut
scene that would have given more screen time

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.570
to The Fashion Twins, Satin and Chenille,
and shown us close up how they were joined

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.260
via a loop in their hair.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.050
The scene kicks off with Poppy checking in
on the Fashion Twins to see if her coronation

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.110
dress is ready.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.490
As well as giving us a look at the coronation
dress, the deleted sequence also flashes through

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:34.580
a series of extra dresses that Satin and Chenille
have designed for Poppy's big day including

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.810
a post-rehearsal gown, formal coronation attire,
an after-coronation party dress, and an after-after

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.210
party muumuu dress.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.980
The scene ends with Poppy shouting, "I want
to wear them all!"

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:49.120
The scene was cut as, although it's very entertaining,
the filmmakers felt it was too long and during

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:54.110
test screenings at DreamWorks some people
thought it made Poppy seem spoiled and obnoxious.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.470
By the way, if you're seen my video on the
deleted characters and rejected concepts in

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:02.090
Trolls, you'll know that in one of the movie's
trailers, when the villainous Chef raids the

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:07.330
Troll village, Poppy is dressed in what looks
like a ceremonial gown, however in the final

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:10.629
film, the same scene shows Poppy wearing her
normal clothes.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:14.510
That's because the party which Poppy was having
at that point in the film was originally going

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:19.720
to be her coronation party rather than just
a celebration party which it was in the final

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.720
film.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.090
There was a deleted song called "Bringing
Back Happy" that I was really disappointed

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.150
didn't make it into the final movie.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.629
It was going to be a villain song for the
Bergen Chef where we'd see her get deliciously

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:35.060
bad as she sings about how she's bringing
back happiness by cooking up the trolls she's

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.060
captured.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.969
It's a fantastic musical number sung by Christine
Baranski who voiced Chef in the movie and

00:02:40.969 --> 00:02:45.300
we get to see some of her villainous plans
to mince up the trolls, whip them into a batter

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.650
and chop them into sushi.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.439
There's a touch of Hollywood's golden age
of musicals including Carmen Miranda, Esther

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:55.529
Williams and choreographer Busby Berkeley
to the song and the dance routine, and I just

00:02:55.529 --> 00:02:56.870
adore it!

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:01.160
It's such a shame it didn't make it into the
movie as villain songs in animations can be

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.970
so memorable – for example, I love Ursula's
Poor Unfortunate Souls in The Little Mermaid

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.260
and, more recently, Tamatoa's Shiny in Moana.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.049
The filmmakers didn't include the song because
they thought it made the Bergen villain too

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:15.359
appealing and not frightening enough.

00:03:15.359 --> 00:03:19.150
Now, what do you think about the deleted scenes
and song and would you like to have seen them

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.150
in the movie?

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.599
And what's your favourite song by a movie
villain?

00:03:22.599 --> 00:03:26.280
Also, would you like to see a Trolls sequel
and what do you think should happen in it?

